  "early_life": {
    "en": "Thorne was born in Logan, Utah and showed early aptitude for science. He earned his Ph.D. at Princeton University under John Archibald Wheeler and became one of the youngest full professors in Caltech's history at age 30.",
    "es": "",
    "pt": "",
    "fr": "",
    "de": "",
    "zh": "",
    "hi": "",
    "ar": "",
    "id": "",
    "ja": ""
  },
  "impact": {
    "en": "Thorne's co-founding of the LIGO project led to one of the most significant experimental achievements in physics: the detection of gravitational waves from merging black holes. His theoretical work on wormholes and time warps also contributed to the scientific accuracy of the film Interstellar.",
